{"file":"Verdict-0.90.2-v2.zip","bytes":1413084,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"verdict","description":"A skeptical QA agent with memory: baseline → delta runs (NEW/REGRESSED/RESOLVED), flaky quarantine with expiry, and evidence-cited release verdicts you can defend.","version":"0.90.2","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/ArtJack/verdict","homepage":"https://github.com/ArtJack/verdict","keywords":["qa","testing","release-gate","regression","flaky-tests","claude-code"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/verdict-flaky-triage/SKILL.md","name":"verdict-flaky-triage","description":"Classify an intermittent test failure with evidence — REAL_DEFECT, STALE_EXPECTATION, BRITTLE_TEST, ENVIRONMENT or FLAKY — and decide quarantine with a mandatory expiry. Use when a test fails one run in five, when CI is \"just flaky\", or before anyone skips a test.","headings":["Verdict: flaky-test triage","Procedure"],"name_hint":"verdict · flaky · triage","description_zh":"用证据把间歇测试失败分为真实缺陷、过时期望、脆弱测试、环境或不稳定，并决定带强制到期时间的隔离，适用于跳过测试前。"},{"path":"skills/verdict-release-risk/SKILL.md","name":"verdict-release-risk","description":"Run a measured, skeptical QA pass on a repository and produce a release verdict you can defend — evidence-cited findings, a stated not-tested list, baseline → delta memory. Use before a merge or release, after a feature lands, or for a scheduled QA run. Reports and specifies; never fixes.","headings":["Verdict: release risk, measured","Setup (once)","The run, in order","The verdict","Hand off in ten lines"],"name_hint":"verdict · release · risk","description_zh":"对仓库做有测量依据的QA，产出引用证据、明确未测试项及基线到改动记忆的发布判断，适用于合并发布、功能落地后或周期检查；只报告和规定，不修复。"},{"path":"skills/verdict-root-cause/SKILL.md","name":"verdict-root-cause","description":"Trace a failure to its root cause with proof, not a story — a four-link chain (symptom, mechanism, origin, class), a counterfactual in an isolated scratch copy, trigger separated from cause, and a diagnosis of where the fix belongs. Use on a failing test, a bug report, or a finding whose cause is disputed.","headings":["Verdict: root cause — the chain, not the label","Procedure"],"name_hint":"verdict · root · cause","description_zh":"用症状、机制、起源和类别四环证据链定位根因，在隔离副本做反事实验证，区分触发条件与原因并判断修复位置，适用于失败测试、缺陷及有争议发现。"},{"path":"skills/verdict-spec-review/SKILL.md","name":"verdict-spec-review","description":"Judge a specification, issue or PRD for testability before any code exists — inventory the requirements, find the untestable, contradictory, unbounded and silent ones with a verbatim quote each, and rewrite the core as Given/When/Then acceptance criteria. Use when a spec is about to be implemented.","headings":["Verdict: spec review, before code","Procedure"],"name_hint":"verdict · spec · 评审","description_zh":"编码前盘点规范、issue或PRD需求，逐项引用不可测试、矛盾、无界或未说明要求，将核心转为Given/When/Then验收标准。"},{"path":"skills/verdict-verify-fix/SKILL.md","name":"verdict-verify-fix","description":"Prove that a fix fixed the defect — re-run the guarding test at the previous commit and at HEAD, re-inject the defect in an isolated scratch copy, and let the harness record fix_verified from measurement, never from a claim. Use after you (the coding agent) fixed a finding and before you call it done.","headings":["Verdict: verify a fix, don't claim it","What the harness measures for you","When you re-inject by hand","What you may not do"],"name_hint":"verdict · 核验 · 修复","description_zh":"在前一提交及HEAD重跑保护测试，并在隔离副本重新注入缺陷，由测试框架测量记录fix_verified，证明修复有效。"}],"commands":[{"path":"commands/baseline.md","name":"baseline","description":"Initialize Verdict for this repo: QA root, project profile, and a baseline run.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/bug.md","name":"bug","description":"Turn a bug report, symptom, log, or user complaint into a structured QA bug report.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/cause.md","name":"cause","description":"Trace a failure, bug, or finding to its root cause — with proof, not a story.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/charter.md","name":"charter","description":"Open a timeboxed exploratory-testing charter with a risk focus.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/flake.md","name":"flake","description":"Classify an intermittent test failure and decide quarantine, with evidence.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/regression.md","name":"regression","description":"Create or run a regression checklist for a change, release, bug fix, or area.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/release.md","name":"release","description":"Run the release QA gate before calling feature or project work done.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/run.md","name":"run","description":"Run Verdict. The front door: reads the tester's memory and picks the right pass — baseline, delta, or a scoped review.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/spec.md","name":"spec","description":"Shift-left review: judge a spec, issue, or PRD for testability — before code exists.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/status.md","name":"status","description":"Read-only QA status from the stored state — no run, no writes, no agent.","headings":[]}],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Verdict","Install","What installs, and when it runs","Quickstart","Why another QA agent","The tested tester","State modes","Commands","The tester's memory, over MCP (optional)"]},{"path":"eval/README.md","headings":["The tested tester","An intermittently-caught trap (open, measured 2026-08-30)","Two halves, and only one of them is free","Layout","Protocol","Paired runs, and rows that read the state","Published results"]},{"path":"eval/fixtures/liar/README.md","headings":["qstats (spec of record)","Requirements","Running"]},{"path":"eval/fixtures/pricer/README.md","headings":["Pricer (spec of record)","Requirements","Running"]},{"path":"eval/fixtures/pricer-ts/README.md","headings":["pricer-ts (spec of record)","Requirements","Running"]},{"path":"eval/fixtures/pricer_clean/README.md","headings":["Pricer (spec of record)","Requirements","Running"]},{"path